Keep recordings review — DONE

**Known fix:** Keep the PCM file in the app’s external files directory for ADB retrieval, and add a RIFF/WAVE header that describes its PCM16 mono data. The plan already specifies both. Android says app-specific external storage needs no storage permission and describes pulling app-scoped output through ADB; Microsoft defines the WAV chunks. [Android storage guidance](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/app-specific), [Android ADB guidance](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/use-cases), [Microsoft RIFF format](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/xaudio2/resource-interchange-file-format--riff-). The manifest’s `allowBackup=false` raises no new storage-permission issue. The plan’s empty-directory `adb shell ls` proves directory access on the S26, but its planned **real-file pull from the non-debuggable Play build** remains the necessary Samsung One UI proof.

1. **HIGH — A quick next take can erase audio before the queued archive copy opens it.** [CapturedAudioFiles.kt:26](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/CapturedAudioFiles.kt:26) queues the copy; [AudioCaptureService.kt:573](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/audio/AudioCaptureService.kt:573) sweeps earlier PCM files when the next take starts. **Fix:** exclude files with a pending archive job from the sweep, or move the closed file to an archive-owned staging path before it can be swept. Test back-to-back takes while the archive worker is held.

2. **HIGH — “Every owner-side ending” is false.** [DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:663](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:663) handles a pre-live ending without deleting its file; the capture-failure branches at lines 688–699 do likewise. The already-ended cancel branch at line 1046 and destroy at line 1235 can abandon one. [AudioCaptureService.kt:717](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/audio/AudioCaptureService.kt:717) can also close a partly created file, then publish a refusal with no path. **Fix:** enumerate these paths in the plan and give each closed file a cleanup/archive owner, or narrow “every take” explicitly. Keep the process-death exclusion separate.

3. **HIGH — Speech can read the file after deletion was queued.** [AsrService.kt:159](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/asr/AsrService.kt:159) submits work to [RecognizerOwner.kt:85](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/asr/RecognizerOwner.kt:85); `readBytes()` runs later on that worker. A timeout can queue deletion at [DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:1165](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionCoordinator.kt:1165) first. **Fix:** revise the plan’s no-race premise and define when the speech worker has finished with the file before deleting it.

4. **MEDIUM — The worker does not guarantee completion after service teardown.** [CapturedAudioFiles.kt:42](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/CapturedAudioFiles.kt:42) uses a daemon thread; [DictationSessionService.kt:251](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/DictationSessionService.kt:251) destroys the service. Android may then kill the process and its thread. [Android process lifecycle](https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/process-lifecycle). **Fix:** state this limit and add recovery for pending PCM and `.part` files on next launch if keeping every completed take is required.

5. **MEDIUM — Retention and capacity need a stronger rule.** [RecordingArchive.kt:41](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/RecordingArchive.kt:41) sorts wall-clock names, so a clock or time-zone change can prune the wrong take; line 43 ignores a failed deletion. A 600-second file is 19.2 MB ([RecordingLimits.kt:43](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/audio/RecordingLimits.kt:43)), and copying before pruning needs space for the old ten, the source, and a new `.part`. **Fix:** retain by a stable take order, check prune results, clean stale `.part` files, and test the full-folder and disk-full cases. State whether “ten” means after successful cleanup.

6. **MEDIUM — The caller list misses a test constructor.** [CapturedAudioFilesTest.kt:19](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/test/java/com/envi/wispr/ui/CapturedAudioFilesTest.kt:19) constructs the class directly and currently lacks the new required `archive` argument. **Fix:** name and update this caller, with a controlled archive fake. The production service and test rig are the other callers found; none appeared in `androidTest` or `debug/`.

7. **MEDIUM — Manual export needs a privacy wording decision.** [PrivacyDisclosure.kt:13](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/privacy/PrivacyDisclosure.kt:13) says audio “never leaves” the phone, while [the plan:20](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/keep-recordings/docs/feature-requests/issue-373-2026-09-25-keep-recordings.md:20) permits an ADB pull. The project `CLAUDE.md` makes the same absolute claim. **Fix:** document the founder’s manual export exception and, before customer exposure, align the privacy copy with the precise promise that the app does not upload audio.

